utside the Warrington County Borough, that one would have expected that further correspond- just so long Will Stockton Heath lack an all-powerful once on the subject would have been unnecessary. I champion to fight her battles in regard to the have, however, waited in vain for the first step towards swing-bridge, and the needed high-level bridge, and the the realization of my dreams and it would appear to level-crossing, and sanitation, and light railways, and the man in the street that there is some deeper motive heaps of other matters which a Parish Council cannot in the opposition than hashitherto appeared, to account long hope to successfully cope with. For instance, for the apathy of our worthy Councillors on the subject. : would that hideous advertisement hoarding; (about Can anyone explain the shelving of the. subject? A , which there has been recent correspondence in " Man- little light would be appreciated. I chester Evening Chronicle"), at Stockton Heath Swing- If one or two of our non-trading Councillors would i bridge, remain in its position very long,, it Stockton take up the subject with half as mum energy and enthu- i Heath residents were within the Borough siasm as has been exhibited by them on the non-trading , This letter has grown rather lengthy, as the subjects question they would earn the gratitude of scores of our ! are much too complex and many-sided to be compressed workingmen, and a change, of subject would I imagine, with any prospect of lucidity. As a practical proposi- be welcomed by most of us.—Yours ttc ' tion, I would suggest that some of the influential resi- 'FRESH AIR. dents of Stockton Heath should form themselves into a permanent Committee, to focus the various local grievances and 'grumblings, and to translate some of these growlings into definite and useful action.—Yours Scc.,</p>
