        <p>The semi-finals for: the Northern Union Cup will be played to day, and I still pin.my faith on Salford and Halifax efor the finals agaihst Oldham and Hall. The Reds, are making their fifth appearance in this round of the Cup-Competition and they well deserve-success.</p>
        <p>Ragged School Band of Hope. 1 The Warrington team to play at Wip,•an to-day is A most successful concert in connection with the a above, was given in the upper schoolroom on Monday.: Hallam, full back ; Fish. 'lsherwood, Dickenson, nd Harris, threeonarters ; Edmunds and Duckworth, half- The chair was taken by Mr. if. Osborne, and his well chosen remarks were greatly enjoyed. There were hacks; Boardman, Morrison, Swift, Forster, Harmer, forwards d Coleman Jolley d dmonson, an , . about 300 people present, and the programme, con- E. sisting of solos, recitations, and dialogues was much ; appreciated by them. At the conclusion -- the adult Wigan" A" will play at Wilderspool. and the home' members gave a dialogue, "The Haunted Room" crowd will have an opportunity of seeing the club's : one and only capture, Mahoney, of Cardiff. The which created roars of laughter. ' Picked team is Knight, full back; Hockenhall,Brooks, Mahoney, and Bailey, threequarters • Hunter and Wilkinson, half-backs: Ashton. Gallop, 'Lunt Roberts, Warburton, Jolley, Fairhurst, and Cresswell, for- wards.</p>
        <p>The second round in the Works Competition com- mences next week,the draw being as follows : Monday Cable Company V Walker's, Tuesday Crosfield's Wire Ropery,Wednesday Rvlands v Tramway, Thurs- day C. L. C. v Pearson and Knowles. The kick-off for these matches is 6-15 p.m. On Friday Fairclough's will play Longford at 10-1.5 am, and an hour- later Naylor's and White Lead will meet. There are also two matches at the same times on Easter Monday, viz, Wilderspool v Loco's or Richmond's. and Fletcher's v Whyman's.</p>
