        <p>Military Appointments. Captain A. de V. Willoughby-Osborne, of the 2nd Battalion of the Prince of Wales" Volunteers,South Lan- cashire Regiment (Dover), was on Saturday appointed adjutant of the 3rd Battalion—the old 4th Royal Lan- cashire Militia ; and Captain T. IT. O'Brien,lst Loyal North Lancashire Regiment (Devonport), son of Mr. W. P. O'Brien, C. 8., was selected for the adjutancy of the 3rd Battalion- the old 3rci Royal Lancashi re Militia. Warrington Training College. Having regard to the great demand for admission into this College the committee have resolved to rent Orfor4.1;1all and open it as a Hostel. This will enable the Oilier of students to be raised to 150. To furnish the Hostel and to enlarge the existing class rooms in the College a .sum of £1,500 will be re- cpired. .•The movement was inaugurated at a meet- ing held at the Training College last week. Lord Derby, the Bishop of Liverpool, the Mayor of War- rington, the Dean of Manchester, the Pri,-,-!pal of Ovren's College and several other gent', Jien were taken over the College by the Principal pointed out the features of interest in each part. Lord Derby and the members of the party were after-,-irds enter- tained at luncheon in the College. .Tll- dcheme met with a very sympathetic consideration and £6OO was promised on that day. It may be hoped that the occupation of the hall for this purpose may be the :means of preserving to the town one of its most inter- esting buildings.</p>
